{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-010", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "US laboratory finds persistent ultraviolet light-induced degradation in solar modules", "content": "<p>While 19 manufacturers received recognition as high achievers in RETC’s 2026 testing sequences, problems with ultraviolet-induced degradation in solar modules persist, while failing “red flag” scores increased in tests for damp heat and thermal cycling.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/latest-retc-solar-module-quality-report-reveals-significant-issues/\">US laboratory finds persistent ultraviolet light-induced degradation in solar modules</a> appeared first on <a", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/latest-retc-solar-module-quality-report-reveals-significant-issues/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-011", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Drought and clear skies drive western North America irradiance gains in May", "content": "<p>In a new weekly update for <b>pv magazine</b>, Solcast, a DNV company, reports that the western half of North America enjoyed positive anomalies in May while the south and east saw widespread deficits.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/drought-and-clear-skies-drive-western-north-america-irradiance-gains-in-may/\">Drought and clear skies drive western North America irradiance gains in May</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Globa", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/drought-and-clear-skies-drive-western-north-america-irradiance-gains-in-may/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-012", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar panel recycling yet to close cost gap before waste surge", "content": "<p>Without mandatory extended producer responsibility, the economics of recycling crystalline silicon modules – which make up roughly 95% of the global installed base – cannot justify the cost gap over landfill on material recovery alone.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/solar-panel-recycling-costs-outpace-recovered-material-value-as-2030-waste-surge-approaches/\">Solar panel recycling yet to close cost gap before waste surge</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://w", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/solar-panel-recycling-costs-outpace-recovered-material-value-as-2030-waste-surge-approaches/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-05-013", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Nigeria runs solar tender for schools, health facilities", "content": "<p>A tender is open in Nigeria covering 32 solar power systems for health care facilities and schools over three regions of the country. The deadline for applications is July 2.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/nigeria-runs-solar-tender-for-schools-health-facilities/\">Nigeria runs solar tender for schools, health facilities </a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/nigeria-runs-solar-tender-for-schools-health-facilities/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "array-2026-06-05-014", "date": "2026-06-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["array"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Researchers test accuracy of simulation tools for floating PV", "content": "<p>Scientists in India have assessed the accuracy of three widely-used simulation tools in predicting the performance of a floating PV plant. The research also found the array is helping to reduce surface water evaporation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/researchers-test-accuracy-of-simulation-tools-for-floating-pv/\">Researchers test accuracy of simulation tools for floating PV</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/05/researchers-test-accuracy-of-simulation-tools-for-floating-pv/", "type": "rss"}]}
